COMPILATION OF: E46M20

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E46M20

   1 a 0000 E46M20:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-42/P2b] CREATE's six-item list with the members of a
   4 a 0006      VISIBLE level-numbered RECORD, which is what RECORD.DCL
   5 a 0006      declares. This object is expected to refuse HERE at the FIXED
   6 a 0006      DECIMAL MEMBER, not at the PUT: bind lays a decimal member out
   7 a 0006      but registers no alias for it ([E2E-39/P2]'s registry is FIXED
   8 a 0006      BINARY(15), POINTER and CHARACTER only). It is probed because it
   9 a 0006      is the only object that says whether DR accepts the member
  10 a 0006      spelling at all, and because the refusal this compiler gives
  11 a 0006      must be shown to come from bind and not from a PUT route this
  12 a 0006      milestone chose to keep closed. */
  13 c 0006   dcl outf file;
  14 c 0006   dcl 1 record,
  15 c 0006     2 name  char(30) varying,
  16 c 0006     2 addr  char(30) varying,
  17 c 0006     2 city  char(20) varying,
  18 c 0006     2 state char(10) varying,
  19 c 0006     2 zip   fixed dec(6),
  20 c 0006     2 phone char(12) varying;
  21 c 0006   open file(outf) stream output title('M20OUT DAT');
  22 c 0023   put file(outf) list(name,addr,city,state,zip,phone);
  23 c 0071   close file(outf);
  24 a 0077 end E46M20;

CODE SIZE = 007A
DATA AREA = 0079
FREE SYMS = 383D
END  COMPILATION
